`reversed()` flips the chain built so far, so call it before `thenComparing` when only the first key should descend. For a `double` key, use `comparingDouble` or `thenComparingDouble`, which work like their `int` versions. Finally, override `toString` so `println(player)` prints readable text instead of `Player@1b6d3586`.

